196
00:14:02.525 --> 00:14:04.491
 No. stealing is a crime.

197
00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:07.161
        But it's not
        a crime to starve.
        That's justice for you.

198
00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:09.213
    Where are you taking him?
 To Riverrun.

199
00:14:09.282 --> 00:14:10.848
        Why Riverrun?

200
00:14:10.917 --> 00:14:13.684
 Steal from the Tullys.
 it's their dungeons
 you rot in.

201
00:14:13.753 --> 00:14:14.836
       Why not kill him?

202
00:14:14.904 --> 00:14:15.970
            For stealing a pig?

203
00:14:16.706 --> 00:14:18.306
 I don't give the orders.

204
00:14:18.374 --> 00:14:19.773
 He must be
 important to someone.

205
00:14:19.842 --> 00:14:22.677
     Sending him with you?
     How important could he be?

206
00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:26.330
              All right.
              have it your way.

207
00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:28.582
                   my lady.

208
00:14:31.621 --> 00:14:33.037
 Do I know you?

209
00:14:33.105 --> 00:14:34.471
                  Have you been
                  to Ashemark?

210
00:14:35.074 --> 00:14:36.140
 No.

211
00:14:36.208 --> 00:14:37.742
        Then you don't know me.

212
00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:40.328
              Do you ever go to
              the river market
              at Salt Rock?

213
00:14:40.413 --> 00:14:41.545
         Is it near Ashemark?

214
00:14:41.614 --> 00:14:43.047
 No.

215
00:14:43.116 --> 00:14:45.183
       I've never been there.

216
00:14:45.252 --> 00:14:46.867
 What do you think
 of these beauties?

217
00:14:48.955 --> 00:14:51.305
             I hope you gave
             them quick deaths.

218
00:14:51.374 --> 00:14:53.374
          Two of them
          we did. yeah.

219
00:14:55.661 --> 00:14:56.744
                          Wait.

220
00:15:00.183 --> 00:15:01.682
      I do know you.

221
00:15:02.585 --> 00:15:05.119
 That's Jaime Lannister.

222
00:15:05.188 --> 00:15:07.288
    I wish someone had told me.
    I wouldn't have had
    to steal that pig.

223
00:15:07.357 --> 00:15:09.791
     If this is the Kingslayer.
     I think I'd know about it.

224
00:15:09.859 --> 00:15:11.959
     How do you know what
     the Kingslayer looks like?

225
00:15:12.028 --> 00:15:13.127
 I was at Whispering Wood.
 I saw him.

226
00:15:13.195 --> 00:15:14.228
 (CHUCKLES)

227
00:15:14.297 --> 00:15:15.563
    They dragged him
    out of the woods

228
00:15:15.632 --> 00:15:17.164
   and threw him
   down before the king.

229
00:15:17.233 --> 00:15:19.383
       He's not the Kingslayer.
       Sorry to disappoint you.

230
00:15:19.452 --> 00:15:21.685
         If he was. I'd only
         be traveling his head.

231
00:15:21.754 --> 00:15:23.754
              I have a question
              for you both.

232
00:15:23.823 --> 00:15:26.190
              And I want you
              to answer it
              at the same time.

233
00:15:26.259 --> 00:15:28.459
              I count to three.
              you both answer.

234
00:15:29.045 --> 00:15:30.644
        What's his name?

235
00:15:31.447 --> 00:15:32.513
            One.

236
00:15:33.583 --> 00:15:35.766
         Two. Three.

237
00:15:37.186 --> 00:15:38.419
                     (GROANS)

238
00:15:40.774 --> 00:15:41.973
         (GRUNTS)

239
00:15:51.434 --> 00:15:52.833
              Two quick deaths.

240
00:15:56.372 --> 00:15:57.555
     (STABBING)
      (GROANING)

241
00:16:12.155 --> 00:16:13.821
              (PANTING)

242
00:16:21.063 --> 00:16:23.297
          Those were Stark men.

243
00:16:23.366 --> 00:16:25.366
 I don't serve the Starks.

244
00:16:26.335 --> 00:16:28.369
 I serve Lady Catelyn.

245
00:16:28.438 --> 00:16:30.337
 I told you I'd take
 you to King's Landing.

246
00:16:30.406 --> 00:16:32.290
 and that's what
 I'm going to do.

247
