          Oh.

499
00:31:50.242 --> 00:31:52.576
 I'm a poor little rich man
 and nobody loves me.

500
00:31:52.644 --> 00:31:55.495
 so I make jokes all the time
 and pay them to laugh.

501
00:31:55.563 --> 00:31:57.163
 Fuck your money.

502
00:31:58.733 --> 00:32:00.384
     Let's leave.
                       Leave?

503
00:32:00.452 --> 00:32:04.187
 Leave King's Landing.
 They tried to kill you.
 They will try again.

504
00:32:04.256 --> 00:32:07.691
 Going into wars.
 fighting soldiers.
 you're terrible at this.

505
00:32:09.578 --> 00:32:12.245
 Let's take a boat to Pentos
 and never come back.

506
00:32:12.314 --> 00:32:13.847
 You don't belong here.

507
00:32:13.915 --> 00:32:15.631
    What would we do in Pentos?

508
00:32:15.700 --> 00:32:17.633
       Eat. drink.

509
00:32:18.770 --> 00:32:20.137
       fuck. live.

510
00:32:24.959 --> 00:32:27.059
         I want to go with you.

511
00:32:27.128 --> 00:32:28.812
 So do it.

512
00:32:28.880 --> 00:32:32.849
 Your father. your sister.
 all these bad people.
 they can't stop you.

513
00:32:32.918 --> 00:32:35.252
 Forget about them.
 Come with me.

514
00:32:37.739 --> 00:32:38.989
                  I can't.

515
00:32:40.492 --> 00:32:42.125
              I do belong here.

516
00:32:43.362 --> 00:32:46.913
          These bad people
          are what I'm good at.

517
00:32:46.982 --> 00:32:48.782
              Outtalking them.
              outthinking them.

518
00:32:49.651 --> 00:32:51.184
                It's what I am.

519
00:32:53.188 --> 00:32:54.687
                 And I like it.

520
00:32:56.358 --> 00:32:59.292
       I like it more than
       anything I've ever done.

521
00:33:04.332 --> 00:33:06.232
        Are you going to leave?

522
00:33:12.540 --> 00:33:14.440
 You have a shit memory.

523
00:33:17.212 --> 00:33:19.479
 I am yours
 and you are mine.

524
00:33:20.915 --> 00:33:21.931
                 (SNIFFLES)

525
00:33:27.622 --> 00:33:29.055
                 (SOBBING)

526
00:33:32.076 --> 00:33:34.261
      SEPTON: In the sight
      of the Seven.

527
00:33:34.329 --> 00:33:37.530
        I hereby seal
        these two souls.

528
00:33:38.901 --> 00:33:42.903
        binding them as
        one for eternity.

529
00:33:46.942 --> 00:33:48.742
      Look upon one another

530
00:33:49.645 --> 00:33:51.311
       and say the words.

531
00:33:55.383 --> 00:33:57.183
 Father. smith...
               Father. smith...

532
00:33:57.252 --> 00:33:59.218
 warrior. mother...
             warrior. mother...

533
00:33:59.287 --> 00:34:02.021
 maiden. crone. stranger.
       maiden. crone. stranger.

534
00:34:02.958 --> 00:34:04.223
 I am hers
 and she is mine...

535
00:34:04.292 --> 00:34:05.525
              I am his
              and he is mine...

536
00:34:05.594 --> 00:34:07.393
 from this day until
 the end of my days.

537
00:34:07.463 --> 00:34:09.195
            from this day until
            the end of my days.

538
00:35:12.227 --> 00:35:13.542
 (BREATHING HEAVILY)

539
00:35:17.649 --> 00:35:19.282
      Is this a riddle?

540
00:35:59.591 --> 00:36:01.490
             Khaleesi!

541
00:36:02.894 --> 00:36:04.227
             Khaleesi!

542
00:36:07.449 --> 00:36:08.715
        JORAH: Khaleesi!

543
00:36:12.887 --> 00:36:16.289
           Are you trying
           to frighten me
           with magic tricks?

544
00:36:16.358 --> 00:36:20.660
        You want me? Here I am.
        Are you afraid
        of a little girl?

545
00:36:20.729 --> 00:36:22.445
      (DRAGONS SCREECHING)

546
00:36:27.352 --> 00:36:29.252
      (DRAGONS SCREECHING)

547
00:36:45.320 --> 00:36:46.986
 HOT PIE: How did
 he find us?

548
00:37:11.846 --> 00:37:13.245
                  What are you
                  doing here?

549
00:37:13.315 --> 00:37:15.348
     Waiting for you.

550
00:37:15.417 --> 00:37:17.983
            How did you know
            we'd come this way?

551
00:37:18.052 --> 00:37:21.788
 After all
 the things you have seen.
 this is your question?

552
00:37:21.856 --> 00:37:24.590
             How did you
             kill those guards?

553
00:37:24.659 --> 00:37:26.826
                   Was it hard?

554
00:37:26.895 --> 00:37:29.595
 No harder than
 taking a new name.
 if you know the way.

555
00:37:29.664 --> 00:37:31.731
                  Show me how.

556
00:37:31.799 --> 00:37:33.650
            I want to be
            able to do it. too.

557
00:37:33.719 --> 00:37:35.752
 If you would learn.
 you must come with me.

558
00:37:35.820 --> 00:37:37.053
                        Where?

559
00:37:37.122 --> 00:37:40.924
 Far and away across
 the Narrow Sea to Braavos.

560
00:37:40.992 --> 00:37:43.576
              My dancing master
              was from Braavos.

561
00:37:43.645 --> 00:37:48.548
 To be a dancing master
 is a special thing.
 but to be a faceless man.

562
00:37:48.616 --> 00:37:50.016
 that is
 something else entirely.

563
00:37:51.469 --> 00:37:53.637
 The girl has many
 names on her lips.

564
00:37:53.705 --> 00:37:56.372
 Joffrey.
 Cersei. Tywin Lannister.

565
00:37:56.441 --> 00:37:58.657
 Ilyn Payne. the Hound.

566
00:37:58.727 --> 00:38:01.127
 Names to offer up
 to the Red God.

567
00:38:02.363 --> 00:38:05.531
 She could offer them all
 one by one.

568
00:38:08.336 --> 00:38:09.668
                I want to.

569
00:38:12.841 --> 00:38:14.240
                   But I can't.

570
00:38:15.377 --> 00:38:17.977
         I need to find
         my brother and mother.

571
00:38:19.464 --> 00:38:20.963
                 And my sister.

572
00:38:22.800 --> 00:38:24.767
       I need to find her. too.

573
00:38:26.054 --> 00:38:28.020
 Then we must part.

574
00:38:28.090 --> 00:38:30.690
 A man has duties as well.

575
00:38:30.758 --> 00:38:32.625
          Here.
                    What is it?

576
00:38:34.096 --> 00:38:35.962
 A coin of great value.

577
00:38:37.599 --> 00:38:39.465
          Could it buy a horse?

578
00:38:39.534 --> 00:38:42.535
 It is not meant for
 the buying of horses.

579
00:38:42.604 --> 00:38:44.336
          Then what good is it?

580
00:38:44.405 --> 00:38:46.705
 If the day comes
 when you must find me again.

581
00:38:46.775 --> 00:38:50.109
 just give that coin
 to any man from Braavos
 and say these words to him.

582
00:38:50.879 --> 00:38:52.495
 "Valar Morghulis."

583
00:38:53.431 --> 00:38:55.031
              Valar Morghulis.

584
00:38:59.187 --> 00:39:00.820
 Please don't go. Jaqen.

585
00:39:04.526 --> 00:39:06.893
               Jaqen is dead.

586
00:39:06.961 --> 00:39:09.245
              Say it again.
              Valar Morghulis.

587
00:39:10.031 --> 00:39:11.630
 Valar Morghulis.

588
00:39:13.318 --> 00:39:14.417
                  Good.

589
00:39:21.743 --> 00:39:23.542
          Farewell. Arya Stark.

590
00:39:48.302 --> 00:39:50.970
 Osha.
 what are you doing?

591
00:40:30.094 --> 00:40:31.795
        (WOLVES WHINING)

592
00:41:04.678 --> 00:41:06.379
 (SOBBING)

593
00:41:15.556 --> 00:41:17.356
 Tell us what medicine
 to get from your chambers.

594
00:41:17.425 --> 00:41:18.824
 We'll make you better.

595
00:41:18.893 --> 00:41:20.226
       I feel just fine.

596
00:41:23.882 --> 00:41:26.999
 They burned it down.
 They burned everything.

597
00:41:27.068 --> 00:41:29.752
            Not everything.
            Not you.

598
00:41:33.408 --> 00:41:35.859
      But they may come back.
      You have to go.

599
00:41:35.927 --> 00:41:37.660
       Put on your
       warmest clothes.

600
00:41:37.729 --> 00:41:39.729
       Pack as much food
       as you can carry
       and go north.

601
00:41:39.797 --> 00:41:41.931
 North's
 the wrong way.

602
00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:43.716
 And Mother and
 brother are south.

603
00:41:43.785 --> 00:41:45.752
       We don't know where.

604
00:41:45.820 --> 00:41:48.755
       There are too many
       enemies in the south.

605
00:41:48.823 --> 00:41:50.823
      Go to the Wall. to Jon.

606
00:41:50.891 --> 00:41:53.593
       He'll look after you
       and let your mother
       know you're safe.

607
00:41:53.661 --> 00:41:56.612
 I don't want to leave you.

608
00:41:56.681 --> 00:42:00.032
       No more than
       I want to leave you.

609
00:42:00.101 --> 00:42:01.450
          I pulled you
          into the world.

610
00:42:03.237 --> 00:42:05.104
           Both of you.

611
00:42:05.173 --> 00:42:08.124
     I've seen both your faces
     almost every day since.

612
00:42:08.193 --> 00:42:10.793
        And for that.
        I consider myself very.

613
00:42:11.696 --> 00:42:13.062
            very lucky.

614
00:42:14.682 --> 00:42:16.832
      Go now with Hodor. Go on.

615
00:42:17.903 --> 00:42:19.635
       I'll be right here.

616
00:42:27.445 --> 00:42:28.544
                          Osha.

617
00:42:29.814 --> 00:42:31.948
         You must protect them.

618
00:42:32.016 --> 00:42:34.149
   You're the only one who can.

619
00:42:36.854 --> 00:42:40.006
   You may have to protect them
   against your own kind.

620
00:42:40.074 --> 00:42:42.508
 I've got no great
 love for my own kind.

621
00:42:43.210 --> 00:42:44.209
                  (GASPS)

622
00:42:45.847 --> 00:42:48.380
 I'll get you
 milk of the poppy.

623
00:42:48.449 --> 00:42:50.215
 Tell me where to find it.

624
00:42:50.284 --> 00:42:52.001
             I don't want
             milk of the poppy.

625
00:43:02.563 --> 00:43:03.863
                 Do it quickly.

626
00:43:36.931 --> 00:43:39.031
           (FOOTSTEPS)

627
00:43:39.100 --> 00:43:40.766
      (DRAGONS SCREECHING)

628
00:45:48.696 --> 00:45:50.512
     (SCREECHING CONTINUES)

629
00:46:17.158 --> 00:46:18.991
         (WIND BLOWING)

630
00:48:44.022 --> 00:48:45.087
 (SNIFFLES)

631
00:48:56.667 --> 00:49:00.168
 Until the sun
 rises in the west
 and sets in the east.

632
00:49:02.873 --> 00:49:05.574
 until the rivers run dry

633
00:49:05.643 --> 00:49:08.711
 and the mountains blow
 in the wind like leaves.

634
00:49:13.383 --> 00:49:14.984
       (DRAGONS SCREECHING)

635
00:49:33.554 --> 00:49:34.704
      (SCREECHING CONTINUES)

636
00:49:50.421 --> 00:49:52.321
        They miss their mother.

637
00:49:53.657 --> 00:49:55.224
      They want to be with you.

638
00:49:55.276 --> 00:49:57.126
 Do you want to
 be with them?

639
00:49:57.194 --> 00:50:00.011
                   You will be.

640
00:50:00.080 --> 00:50:04.099
   When your dragons were born.
   our magic was born again.

641
00:50:04.168 --> 00:50:05.651
 It is strongest
 in their presence.

642
00:50:06.554 --> 00:50:08.904
            And they are
            strongest in yours.

643
00:50:10.207 --> 00:50:12.074
         You will be with them.

644
00:50:12.910 --> 00:50:15.010
        through winter. summer.

645
00:50:15.980 --> 00:50:18.280
               winter again.

646
00:50:18.349 --> 00:50:21.016
             Across a thousand.
             thousand seasons

647
00:50:21.085 --> 00:50:22.718
    you will be with them.

648
00:50:22.787 --> 00:50:25.904
    And we will be with you
    until time comes to an end.

649
00:50:25.973 --> 00:50:27.640
      (DRAGONS SCREECHING)

650
00:50:31.896 --> 00:50:34.763
            Welcome home.
            Daenerys Stormborn.

651
00:50:35.666 --> 00:50:37.299
         This is
         not my home.

652
00:50:37.367 --> 00:50:41.070
 My home is across the sea.
 where my people
 are waiting for me.

653
00:50:41.138 --> 00:50:42.988
           They will be
           waiting a long time.

654
00:51:00.975 --> 00:51:02.240
       Dracarys.

655
00:51:18.392 --> 00:51:20.058
          (PYAT PREE SCREAMING)

656
00:51:42.933 --> 00:51:44.567
         (CHAINS BREAKING)

657
00:51:50.858 --> 00:51:53.592
           YGRITTE: We should
           be there by sundown.

658
00:51:53.660 --> 00:51:57.662
        Won't be a fun night
        for you. Mance knows
        how to make crows sing.

659
00:52:00.434 --> 00:52:03.752
 If you know what to say.
 you might just make it
 through the night.

660
00:52:06.523 --> 00:52:09.024
             Not talking's
             not the way to go.

661
00:52:10.861 --> 00:52:12.428
 Careful with that.

662
00:52:12.496 --> 00:52:14.396
 You might cut yourself.

663
00:52:15.499 --> 00:52:17.433
 Never swung
 a sword before. have you?

664
00:52:17.501 --> 00:52:19.201
 You look like
 a baby with a rattle.

665
00:52:19.270 --> 00:52:20.318
                Enough of that!

666
00:52:21.639 --> 00:52:22.638
             (GRUNTS)

667
00:52:24.542 --> 00:52:25.541
                     (SHOUTS)

668
00:52:26.210 --> 00:52:27.459
               (GRUNTING)

669
00:52:31.131 --> 00:52:33.131
                     Stop!
      Why. traitor?

670
00:52:33.200 --> 00:52:36.401
 So you can give
 Mance Rayder an invitation
 to Castle Black?

671
00:52:36.470 --> 00:52:37.636
            Let 'em fight.

672
00:52:39.607 --> 00:52:41.056
     (GRUNTING)

673
00:52:58.275 --> 00:53:01.343
        That's it?
        That's what you can do?

674
00:53:01.412 --> 00:53:02.928
             You little shit.

675
00:53:08.336 --> 00:53:10.052
 Your traitor father
 teach you that?

676
00:53:13.941 --> 00:53:15.791
 Or was it your whore mother?

677
00:53:25.936 --> 00:53:27.269
                 (PANTING)

678
00:53:27.337 --> 00:53:28.670
 (GROANS)

679
00:53:34.327 --> 00:53:37.496
 We are
 the watchers on the Wall.

680
00:53:50.761 --> 00:53:53.479
 You can tell Mance

681
00:53:53.547 --> 00:53:56.114
 that's the man who
 killed Qhorin Halfhand.

682
00:54:10.564 --> 00:54:12.631
                Burn the body.
            MAN: Aye.

683
00:54:12.700 --> 00:54:15.634
       You don't want this
       one coming back for you.

684
00:54:29.066 --> 00:54:30.799
 Come along. Jon Snow.

685
00:54:56.994 --> 00:54:59.628
 Time to meet
 the King-beyond-the-Wall.

686
00:55:46.326 --> 00:55:47.692
      What the...

687
00:55:49.964 --> 00:55:51.046
                    (SCREECHES)

688
00:55:54.518 --> 00:55:56.317
      DOREAH: Khaleesi. please.

689
00:55:56.386 --> 00:55:58.153
            He said you'd never
            leave Qarth alive.

690
00:55:58.221 --> 00:55:59.254
                DAENERYS: Come.

691
00:56:31.087 --> 00:56:32.320
             Nothing.

692
00:56:40.414 --> 00:56:43.965
         Thank you.
         Xaro Xhoan Daxos.

693
00:56:44.034 --> 00:56:46.367
    Thank you for
    teaching me this lesson.

694
00:56:49.573 --> 00:56:53.358
            I am king of Qarth.
            I can help you now.
            truly help you.

695
00:56:53.426 --> 00:56:54.793
 We can take the Iron Throne.

696
00:56:54.862 --> 00:56:56.077
 I'll bring you
 a thousand ships.

697
00:56:56.146 --> 00:56:57.345
      Please. Khaleesi.
      I beg you.

698
00:56:57.414 --> 00:56:59.230
 All that you have dreamed
 is within your reach!

699
00:56:59.299 --> 00:57:00.966
 I beg you. please!

700
00:57:02.536 --> 00:57:03.735
                     Khaleesi.

701
00:57:03.803 --> 00:57:04.969
         Please! Please!

702
00:57:05.039 --> 00:57:06.872
    XARO: Khaleesi!
         (DOOR CLANKS)

703
00:57:27.094 --> 00:57:28.626
                It's all a lie.

704
00:57:30.030 --> 00:57:31.996
 Looks real enough to me.

705
00:57:36.636 --> 00:57:38.670
 Real enough to buy a ship?

706
00:57:40.074 --> 00:57:42.674
             Aye. a small ship.

707
00:57:53.187 --> 00:57:54.837
           (CHEERING)

708
00:57:58.209 --> 00:57:59.674
                   (PURRING)

709
00:58:02.779 --> 00:58:04.179
                    (SCREECHES)

710
00:58:12.739 --> 00:58:14.472
        (WIND HOWLING)

711
00:58:27.037 --> 00:58:30.238
 I thought we were
 coming north to
 fight wildlings.

712
00:58:33.243 --> 00:58:34.710
 Is this goat?

713
00:58:35.546 --> 00:58:38.080
          It's moose.

714
00:58:38.148 --> 00:58:41.049
 People shouldn't live
 anywhere you need to
 burn shit to keep warm.

715
00:58:41.118 --> 00:58:44.219
            Well. you
            see a tree.
            let me know.

716
00:58:47.373 --> 00:58:49.574
            If you step back
            and think about it.

717
00:58:49.643 --> 00:58:51.876
    the thing about Gilly
    that's so interesting is...

718
00:58:51.945 --> 00:58:52.978
          Just bloody kill me.

719
00:58:53.046 --> 00:58:54.512
                     No. truly.

720
00:58:54.581 --> 00:58:57.315
        The thing about her
        that I find
        so interesting

721
00:58:57.383 --> 00:59:00.251
      is that after all that
      Craster's done to her.

722
00:59:00.320 --> 00:59:02.621
         she's still got
         hope that life
         might get better.

723
00:59:02.689 --> 00:59:05.874
 The thing about Gilly
 that you find
 so interesting

724
00:59:05.943 --> 00:59:09.144
 is that she said
 six words to you.

725
00:59:09.213 --> 00:59:12.263
     And the thing about you
     that I find so interesting

726
00:59:12.333 --> 00:59:14.199
         is absolutely nothing.

727
00:59:14.268 --> 00:59:16.001
          (HORN BLOWING)

728
00:59:17.671 --> 00:59:20.455
     It's Jon and the Halfhand.
     They're back.

729
00:59:22.642 --> 00:59:23.858
          (HORN BLOWS)

730
00:59:25.128 --> 00:59:26.895
         Two blasts
         is wildlings.

731
00:59:26.963 --> 00:59:29.831
 You're not fighting
 them alone. Come on.

732
00:59:29.900 --> 00:59:31.567
         (HORN BLOWING)

733
00:59:34.121 --> 00:59:35.737
 GRENN: Three blasts?

734
00:59:35.805 --> 00:59:37.038
           Run!

735
00:59:43.764 --> 00:59:45.964
      Wait! Wait for me!

736
00:59:49.803 --> 00:59:50.953
         Grenn!

737
00:59:52.556 --> 00:59:53.621
         Edd!

738
00:59:59.045 --> 01:00:00.361
    (HIGH-PITCHED WHISTLING)

739
01:00:25.221 --> 01:00:26.721
        (BREATHING HEAVILY)

740
01:01:18.258 --> 01:01:19.674
                     (SOBBING)

741
01:01:24.097 --> 01:01:25.697
                  (SHRIEKING)

742
01:01:35.476 --> 01:01:37.408
            (SHRIEKING)

743
01:01:47.754 --> 01:01:49.488
           (SHRIEKING)

744
01:01:58.298 --> 01:01:59.931
           (SHRIEKING)

744
